WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Speaker 1: Hey, everybody. Producer Pat here,&nbsp;
bringing you some holiday cheer on this Christmas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:09.200
Eve. Let's get back into the news story, starting&nbsp;
with this one about the 2024 presidential race.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.240
A new poll finds that a majority of Americans&nbsp;
don't want to see Donald Trump run for president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.400
again. But also a majority of Americans. They&nbsp;
don't want to see Joe Biden run for president&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.600
again, either. The poll comes to us from Echelon&nbsp;
Insights, and the results are that 55 percent of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:29.200
respondents don't want to see Donald Trump seek&nbsp;
the presidency again in 2024. And that's great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:34.720
news, right? But also statistically just as many&nbsp;
54 percent of respondents they say that they don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.320
want to see Joe Biden run again as well. Now on&nbsp;
the approval side, when you flip the question&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.680
and ask, Do you want Trump to one run? Do you want&nbsp;
Biden to run? There does seem to be more support&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.560
for Trump running than Biden. 39 percent give&nbsp;
Trump the go ahead, whereas only 34 percent say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:55.680
the same thing about Biden. So the question is&nbsp;
three years out from the next presidential race.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.680
Is this cause for concern for Democrats? I think&nbsp;
part of this is that Americans are saying they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.880
want to see new faces, you know, if Trump runs&nbsp;
again. This will be his third attempt. He's been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:12.320
nonstop in the political atmosphere ever since&nbsp;
2015. Biden, he's been in the Senate forever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:15.680
and then he was vice president. He ran a bunch&nbsp;
of different presidential campaigns. And then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.160
of course, now he is the president. So, you know,&nbsp;
it's just time to see some new people here. We're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.880
sort of sick of these guys and we don't want to&nbsp;
see an exact repeat of the 2020 election, after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:31.120
all. And part of this also is the fact that they&nbsp;
are quite up there in age, right? If Trump gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.320
elected in 2024, he's going to be seventy eight by&nbsp;
the time he's elected and 82 by the time he leaves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:41.200
office. And if Joe Biden gets reelected, he's&nbsp;
going to be 82 at the start of his second term.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.840
And 86 by the time that he's out of office.&nbsp;
And we know that of course, people now are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:51.520
living longer lives these days, and you can have&nbsp;
elderly people who are capable of doing the job.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:56.000
But some may say 80s, that's kind of pushing&nbsp;
it. Maybe we need some younger blood in there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.160
but I think this really comes down to at the end&nbsp;
of the day. The most important factor in all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:06.320
this is that the hardcore Trump people who make up&nbsp;
somewhere between 35 to 40 percent, unfortunately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.800
of the country, they want him no matter&nbsp;
what, right? They don't care about Ted Cruz,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:16.240
they don't care about Nikki Haley. You know, maybe&nbsp;
Ron DeSantis is OK, but only as a back up option&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.440
if Trump doesn't want to run. And so that's, I&nbsp;
think, why we're seeing the numbers show that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:26.400
39 percent of people say they do want Trump to&nbsp;
run. Those are the hardcore Trump supporters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.840
whereas there's people who support&nbsp;
Joe Biden, but they don't have the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:34.960
same sort of cult of personality view of&nbsp;
him, right? Biden doesn't have this sort of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.240
appeal that Trump does among his base of&nbsp;
supporters. Biden's approval rating right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:46.240
now is in the low to mid 40s, which is not great.&nbsp;
It's also not terrible. But the number who wants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:51.520
to see him run again is again 34 percent, which&nbsp;
is substantially lower than what his approval&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:55.520
numbers at. So that suggests to me that there's&nbsp;
a good amount of people who are saying, Yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:00.480
I like what Biden is doing, but he's replaceable,&nbsp;
right? Like if you give us Kamala Harris,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:06.400
if you give us Pete Buttigieg or Elizabeth Warren&nbsp;
or whoever else we'll like them to, because at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:11.120
end of the day, it's more about the cause than the&nbsp;
person. And then also in addition, you don't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:16.000
to worry about the age factor. You don't have to&nbsp;
worry about age or fitness or anything like that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.920
So that's my take away. The Trump people are&nbsp;
wrapped up in the cult of Trump, and the Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.080
people don't care about Biden specifically. They&nbsp;
just want to move the causes forward. And I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:28.720
there's a real question whether Biden will run&nbsp;
again, mainly because of the age factor. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.000
that if he chooses not to run again, obviously&nbsp;
there will be a primary in the Democratic field.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.080
There's a possibility that Kamala Harris being&nbsp;
the vice president, she caught, she gets that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.640
coronation treatment that Hillary Clinton got&nbsp;
back in 2016. Hopefully that doesn't happen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:48.640
and hopefully we get some progressive challenges&nbsp;
in there to make it not so easy to fight for her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:54.480
But ultimately, if Biden chooses to run again,&nbsp;
he'll get the nomination. And I think Trump is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:58.480
definitely running again. Also, I mean, he's&nbsp;
dropping all these hints as to how he's going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:03.280
launch another campaign. I know some people&nbsp;
like Michael Cohen, for example, he's saying in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:07.680
including on the show, he said, I don't think that&nbsp;
Trump is going to run again because he's terrified&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:12.720
of losing for a second time. He doesn't want to be&nbsp;
seen as a two time loser. And the excuse of voter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.680
fraud, if he does lose, isn't going to work again.&nbsp;
But I just don't buy that like it. First of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:22.640
I think that if Trump does run again, he's going&nbsp;
to have a substantial chance at winning. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:28.720
he's actually going to get better odds of winning&nbsp;
than he did in 2016 or 2020. And if he does lose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:32.640
then he'll just tell his voters, Yeah, it was&nbsp;
voter fraud, and they're already primed to believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:37.440
the voter fraud stuff. They'll just say, like, OK,&nbsp;
well, they got us again, those Democrats rigging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:41.680
their elections. So, you know, I don't think Trump&nbsp;
is really worried about anything there. It's sort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:46.800
of a heads. I win tails. You lose sort of scenario&nbsp;
where either he wins the presidency or he just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:51.600
says once again that he got cheated. So the bottom&nbsp;
line is most Americans don't want to see Trump run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:56.720
again. Most Americans don't want to see Biden run&nbsp;
again. And yet there's still a halfway decent shot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.720 --> 00:06:01.600
that we see yet another Trump Biden match up a.&nbsp;
A repeat of the last election cycle in twenty.

